          <outline text="Chicken Bacon Ranch Wraps (Meal Prep) ">
            <outline text="Ingredients:">
              <outline text="1.3 Kg skinless and boneless chicken breast (raw weight)" />
              <outline text="2 tsp chili powder" />
              <outline text="1.5 tsp cumin" />
              <outline text="1 tsp salt" />
              <outline text="1 tsp black pepper" />
              <outline text="2 tsp smoked paprika" />
              <outline text="1 tsp garlic powder" />
              <outline text="1 tsp onion powder" />
              <outline text="1/2 tsp oregano (or 1 packet of store-bought taco seasoning)" />
              <outline text="500 g low-fat cottage cheese" />
              <outline text="2 tbsp ranch seasoning" />
              <outline text="1 tsp chipotle in adobo sauce" />
              <outline text="1/2 juiced lime" />
              <outline text="2 diced garlic cloves" />
              <outline text="45 ml light mayonnaise" />
              <outline text="200 g light grated mozzarella (Bega 50% less fat grated cheese)" />
              <outline text="Chives" />
              <outline text="10 tortillas (Simpsons Pantry large low carb protein tortillas)" />
              <outline text="1 kg cooked white rice (mixed with cilantro/coriander - 100 g per burrito, amount can be adjusted to your preference)" />
            </outline>
            <outline text="Directions:">
              <outline text="Preparing the Chicken:">
                <outline text="Season the chicken breast with chili powder, cumin, salt, black pepper, smoked paprika, garlic powder, onion powder, and oregano (or taco seasoning)." />
                <outline text="&lt;i&gt;Note: You can also use a store-bought taco seasoning packet instead of individual spices.&lt;/i&gt;" />
              </outline>
              <outline text="Making the Filling:">
                <outline text="In a bowl, combine cottage cheese, ranch seasoning, chipotle in adobo sauce, lime juice, garlic cloves, mayonnaise, and grated mozzarella. Mix well." />
              </outline>
              <outline text="Assembling the Burritos:">
                <outline text="Warm each tortilla on a pan over low heat for 30 seconds on each side to prevent breaking." />
                <outline text="Spread a layer of the chicken filling on each tortilla." />
                <outline text="Top with a scoop of rice and a sprinkle of chives." />
                <outline text="Roll up the tortillas tightly." />
              </outline>
              <outline text="Storing and Reheating:">
                <outline text=" * Storing: Wrap individual burritos in foil and freeze." />
              </outline>
              <outline text="Reheating:">
                <outline text="   * Microwave: Remove the burrito from foil, wrap in a paper towel, and microwave for 2 minutes to thaw and warm the middle." />
                <outline text="   * Air Fryer: Air fry at 190°C/375°F for 5-8 minutes (time may vary depending on the air fryer)." />
                <outline text="   * Oven: Bake at 190°C/375°F for 5-8 minutes (time may vary)." />
                <outline text="   * Pan Fry: Fry the burrito in a pan over medium heat until heated through and crispy." />
              </outline>
              <outline text="Additional Tips:">
                <outline text=" You can adjust the amount of rice and filling to your preference." />
                <outline text=" For a spicier filling, add more chili powder or chipotle in adobo sauce." />
              </outline>
            </outline>
            <outline text="" />
          </outline>
