          <outline text="Sweet Potato Quinoa Chili">
            <outline text="Ingredients">
              <outline text="1 ½ tablespoons olive oil (divided)" />
              <outline text="1 medium red onion (chopped)" />
              <outline text="4 cloves garlic (minced)" />
              <outline text="1.5 pounds sweet potatoes (about 2 medium (4 cups chopped), peeled and chopped into ½-inch pieces)" />
              <outline text="2 tablespoons chili powder" />
              <outline text="1 tablespoon cumin" />
              <outline text="1 teaspoon dried oregano" />
              <outline text="1/2 teaspoon smoked paprika" />
              <outline text="½ teaspoon salt" />
              <outline text="1/4 teaspoon black pepper" />
              <outline text="6 ounce can tomato paste" />
              <outline text="28 ounce can diced tomatoes" />
              <outline text="2 1/2 cups vegetable broth (plus more as needed)" />
              <outline text="¾ cup quinoa (rinsed and drained)" />
              <outline text="2 15 ounce cans black beans (rinsed and drained)" />
            </outline>
            <outline text="Directions">
              <outline text="Heat 1 tablespoon olive oil in a large pot or Dutch oven over medium-low heat. Add the onion and cook, stirring occasionally, until softened, 2-3 minutes. Add the garlic and stir for 30 seconds." />
              <outline text="Increase the heat to medium and add the remaining ½ tablespoon olive oil and the chopped sweet potatoes to the pot. Cook for 5 minutes, stirring occasionally." />
              <outline text="Stir in the chili powder, cumin, oregano, smoked paprika, salt, pepper and tomato paste. Cook, stirring, for 2-3 minutes to deepen the flavors of the spices and tomato paste." />
              <outline text="Stir in the the diced tomatoes, broth, quinoa and black beans." />
              <outline text="Reduce heat to a low simmer and cook for about 25 minutes, until the quinoa and sweet potatoes are soft." />
              <outline text="Serve with toppings as desired: Greek yogurt or sour cream, avocado, shredded cheese, cilantro, chopped red onion, green onion. A squeeze of fresh lime juice also brightens up the flavors." />
              <outline text="NOTES" />
              <outline text="Be sure to chop the sweet potatoes into 1/2-inch cubes. The smaller cubes will cook faster than larger pieces." />
              <outline text="This chili is not very spicy. If you want more heat, add 2 or more teaspoons of adobo sauce from a can of chipotle peppers in adobo, until your chili is as spicy as you want it." />
              <outline text="Read the post above for instructions to make this chili in the slow cooker or Instant Pot." />
            </outline>
            <outline text="Source">
              <outline text="&lt;a href=&quot;https://kristineskitchenblog.com/sweet-potato-black-bean-chili-quinoa/&quot;&gt;https://kristineskitchenblog.com/&lt;/a&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://kristineskitchenblog.com/sweet-potato-black-bean-chili-quinoa/&quot;&gt;sweet&lt;/a&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://kristineskitchenblog.com/sweet-potato-black-bean-chili-quinoa/&quot;&gt;-&lt;/a&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://kristineskitchenblog.com/sweet-potato-black-bean-chili-quinoa/&quot;&gt;potato&lt;/a&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://kristineskitchenblog.com/sweet-potato-black-bean-chili-quinoa/&quot;&gt;-black-bean-&lt;/a&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://kristineskitchenblog.com/sweet-potato-black-bean-chili-quinoa/&quot;&gt;chili&lt;/a&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://kristineskitchenblog.com/sweet-potato-black-bean-chili-quinoa/&quot;&gt;-quinoa/&lt;/a&gt;" />
            </outline>
          </outline>
