              <outline text="#mexican " />
            </outline>
            <outline text="Fettuccine Alfredo">
              <outline text="#Italian " />
            </outline>
            <outline text="Patty Melts">
              <outline text="Ingredients" _note="Serves 4">
                <outline text="10 slices hearty rye sandwich bread" _note="To make sure that the melts hold together, use rye bread that's sliced about ½ inch thick." />
                <outline text="whole milk" _note="2 tablespoons " />
                <outline text="onion powder" _note="¾ teaspoon" />
                <outline text="salt" _note="1¼ teaspoons" />
                <outline text="pepper" _note="½ teaspoon" />
                <outline text="ground beef" _note="1 ½ pounds (85 percent lean)&#10;" />
                <outline text="unsalted butter" _note="3 tablespoons " />
                <outline text="2 onions" _note="halved and sliced thin" />
                <outline text="Swiss cheese" _note="8 ounces, shredded (2 cups)&#10;" />
              </outline>
              <outline text="Directions">
                <outline text="1. Adjust oven rack to middle position and heat oven to 200 degrees. Tear 2 slices bread into ½-inch pieces. Using potato masher, mash torn bread, milk, onion powder, ¾ teaspoon salt, and pepper in large bowl until smooth. Add beef and gently knead until well combined. Divide mixture into 4 equal portions. Shape each portion into 6 by 4-inch oval." />
                <outline text="2. Melt 1 tablespoon butter in large nonstick skillet over medium-high heat. Add 2 patties and cook until well browned on first side, about 5 minutes. Transfer to large plate, browned side up, and repeat with remaining 2 patties." />
                <outline text="3. Pour off all but 1 teaspoon fat from skillet. Add onions and remaining ½ teaspoon salt and cook, stirring occasionally, until golden brown, 8 to 10 minutes. Arrange patties, browned side up, on top of onions, pouring any accumulated juices into skillet. Reduce heat to medium and cook, shaking skillet occasionally, until onions are tender and patties are cooked through, about 5 minutes." />
                <outline text="4. Divide 1 cup cheese among 4 slices bread. Top with patties, onions, remaining 1 cup cheese, and remaining 4 slices bread. Wipe skillet clean with paper towels. Melt 1 tablespoon butter in now-empty skillet over medium heat. Add 2 sandwiches and cook until golden brown and cheese is melted, 3 to 4 minutes per side. Place on rimmed baking sheet and transfer to oven to keep warm. Repeat with remaining I tablespoon butter and remaining 2 sandwiches. Serve." />
              </outline>
              <outline text="" />
            </outline>
            <outline text="Grandpa’s Garlic Glazed Chicken">
              <outline text="Ingredients" _note="8 Servings&#10;">
                <outline text="soy sauce" _note="½ cup low-sodium&#10;" />
                <outline text="light brown sugar" _note="2 tablespoons firmly packed" />
                <outline text="distilled white vinegar" _note="1½ tablespoons " />
                <outline text="4 cloves garlic" _note="crushed" />
                <outline text="1 bay leaf" />
                <outline text="whole peppercorns" _note="½ teaspoon&#10;" />
                <outline text="1 whole chicken" _note="(5-pound), giblets removed" />
                <outline text="8 cloves garlic" _note="grated" />
                <outline text="unsalted butter" _note="1 cup, softened and divided&#10;" />
                <outline text="kosher salt" _note="3½ teaspoons, divided&#10;" />
                <outline text="ground black pepper" _note="¾ teaspoon, divided" />
                <outline text="2 heads garlic" _note="halved crosswise" />
                <outline text="fresh thyme" _note="6 sprigs " />
                <outline text="unsalted butter" _note="2 tablespoons, melted&#10;" />
                <outline text="chicken broth" _note="3 tablespoons" />
              </outline>
              <outline text="Directions">
                <outline text="1. Preheat oven to 425°. Place a roasting rack in a large roasting pan." />
                <outline text="2. In a medium saucepan, combine soy Sauce, brown sugar, vinegar, crushed garlic, bay leaf, and peppercorns. Simmer over medium heat, stirring frequently, until reduced and slightly thickened, 6 to 8 minutes. Reserve 1 tablespoon glaze; set aside." />
                <outline text="3. Thoroughly pat chicken dry. In a small bowl, stir together grated garlic, 1/4 cup butter, 2½ teaspoons salt, and 1/4 teaspoon pepper. Rub butter mixture under skin. Sprinkle chicken cavity with 1/2 teaspoon salt and 1/4 teaspoon pepper; stuff cavity with heads of garlic and thyme. Tie legs together with kitchen twine. Place chicken in prepared pan. Brush with melted butter, and sprinkle with remaining ½ teaspoon salt and remaining ¼ teaspoon pepper." />
                <outline text="4. Roast until skin is golden brown and a meat thermometer inserted in thickest portion of thigh registers 165°, 1 hour and 15 minutes to 1 hour and 30 minutes, brushing chicken with soy glaze during last 5 minutes. Remove from oven; brush with remaining glaze. Let rest for 20 minutes." />
                <outline text="5. In a small saucepan, bring broth and reserved 1 tablespoon glaze to a boil. Remove from heat; gradually whisk in remaining ¾ cup butter until smooth. Serve immediately with chicken." />
              </outline>
              <outline text="" />
            </outline>
            <outline text="Grilled Cheese">
              <outline text="Ingredients #needsattention " />
              <outline text="Directions" />
              <outline text="Also Try &lt;a href=&quot;https://workflowy.com/#/e88d6d1e2f6b&quot;&gt;Grown-Up &lt;/a&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://workflowy.com/#/e88d6d1e2f6b&quot;&gt;Grilled&lt;/a&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://workflowy.com/#/e88d6d1e2f6b&quot;&gt; &lt;/a&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://workflowy.com/#/e88d6d1e2f6b&quot;&gt;Cheese&lt;/a&gt;" />
              <outline text="#vegetarian " />
            </outline>
            <outline text="Grown-Up Grilled Cheese">
              <outline text="Ingredients">
                <outline text="7 ounces aged cheddar cheese" _note="cut into2 4 equal pieces, room temperature" />
                <outline text="2 ounces Brie cheese" _note="rind removed " />
                <outline text="2 tablespoons dry white wine or vermouth" />
                <outline text="4 teaspoons minced shallot" />
                <outline text="3 tablespoons unsalted butter " _note="softened" />
                <outline text="1 teaspoon Dijon mustard" />
                <outline text="8 slices hearty white sandwich bread" />
              </outline>
              <outline text="Directions">
                <outline text="Process cheddar, Brie, and wine in food processor until smooth paste forms, 20 to 30 seconds. Add shallot and pulse to combine, 3 to 5 pulses. Combine butter and mustard in small bowl." />
                <outline text="Working on parchment paper-lined counter, spread mustard butter evenly over 1 side of bread. Flip 4 slices and spread cheese mixture evenly over slices. Top with remaining 4 slices, buttered sides up." />
                <outline text="Preheat 12-inch nonstick skillet over medium heat for 2 minutes. (Droplets of water should just sizzle when flicked onto skillet.) Place 2 sandwiches in skillet; reduce heat to medium-low and cook until both sides are crispy and golden brown, 6 to 9 minutes per side, moving sandwiches as necessary to ensure even browning. Remove sandwiches from skillet and let stand for 2 minutes before serving." />
                <outline text="Repeat with remaining 2 sandwiches." />
              </outline>
              <outline text="Source: Cook's Illustrated Cook Book" />
            </outline>
            <outline text="Gyro &amp; Tabouli">
              <outline text="Ingredients #needsattention " />
              <outline text="Directions" />
              <outline text="#greek" />
            </outline>
            <outline text="Margherita Pasta">
              <outline text="Ingredients">
                <outline text="spaghetti " _note="1 lb or pasta of choice" />
                <outline text="olive oil" _note="2 tablespoons " />
                <outline text="butter" _note="2 tablespoons" />
                <outline text="1/4 onion" _note="chopped" />
                <outline text="6 Roma tomatoes" _note="chopped divided" />
                <outline text="4-6 garlic cloves" _note="minced" />
                <outline text="all-purpose flour" _note="1/4 cup " />
                <outline text="low sodium chicken broth" _note="1 1/2 cups" />
                <outline text="milk" _note="1 1/2 cups&#10;" />
                <outline text="chicken bouillon" _note="2 teaspoons " />
                <outline text="dried parsley" _note="1 teaspoon " />
                <outline text="dried oregano, dried basil, salt" _note="1/2 tsp EACH" />
                <outline text="pepper, red pepper flakes" _note="1/4 tsp EACH" />
                <outline text="freshly grated Parmesan cheese" _note="1/2 cup " />
                <outline text="shredded mozzarella cheese" _note="1/2 cup " />
                <outline text="cream cheese" _note="2 oz. , softened (I use 1/3 less fat)" />
                <outline text="basil" _note="1/4 cup loosely packed, chopped&#10;" />
              </outline>
              <outline text="Directions">
                <outline text="Cook pasta al dente according to package directions in generously salted water. Remove 1 cup pasta water before draining." />
                <outline text="Melt butter in olive oil over medium-low heat in a large skillet. Increase heat to medium and add onions and HALF of the tomatoes and sauté for 5 minutes. Add garlic and cook an additional 30 seconds. Sprinkle in flour and cook while stirring for 2 minutes (it will be thick)." />
                <outline text="Turn heat to low then slowly whisk in chicken broth, then milk, stirring constantly until smooth. Turn heat to medium high and bring the sauce to a simmer. Stir in spices and continue to simmer until slightly thickened, stirring occasionally." />
                <outline text="Reduce heat to low and stir in Parmesan cheese until melted, followed by mozzarella cheese until melted, followed by cream cheese until melted." />
                <outline text="Stir in remaining tomatoes and fresh basil. Stir in pasta until well coated, adding additional reserved pasta water a little at a time if needed to reach desired consistency. Taste and season with additional salt, pepper and/or red pepper flakes to taste." />
                <outline text="Garnish with freshly grated Parmesan Cheese and additional basil if desired." />
              </outline>
              <outline text="" />
              <outline text="Source">
                <outline text="&lt;a href=&quot;https://carlsbadcravings.com/margherita-pasta-recipe/&quot;&gt;https://carlsbadcravings.com/margherita-pasta-recipe/&lt;/a&gt;" />
              </outline>
            </outline>
