            <outline text="So Delizioso Chicken Cutlets" _note="with Cheesy Mashed Potatoes and Tomato Zucchini Jumble">
              <outline text="Ingredients">
                <outline text="1 lemon" />
                <outline text="Chicken Cutlets" _note="10 oz " />
                <outline text="Italian Seasoning" _note="1 TBSP " />
                <outline text="Yukon Gold Potatoes" _note="16 oz&#10;" />
                <outline text="Scallions" _note="2 units " />
                <outline text="Italian Cheese Blend" _note="1/2 cup" />
                <outline text="Grape Tomatoes" _note="4 oz " />
                <outline text="1 shallot" />
                <outline text="1 zucchini" />
                <outline text="chicken stock concentrate" _note="1 unit?? #needsattention &#10;" />
                <outline text="Also">
                  <outline text="5 tsp Olive Oil" />
                  <outline text="3 TBSP butter" />
                  <outline text="Salt &amp; Pepper" />
                  <outline text="Utensils" _note="Paper Towel • Zester • Medium Pot • Strainer • Potato Masher • Large Pan • Large Bowl" />
                </outline>
              </outline>
              <outline text="Directions">
                <outline text="Wash and dry all produce. Zest and halve lemon. Pat chicken dry with a paper towel. Place in a large bowl or zip-close bag along with zest, juice from one lemon half, 1½ tsp Italian seasoning (we’ll use the rest later), and a large drizzle of olive oil. Season with salt and pepper. Toss to coat, then set aside." />
                <outline text="Cut potatoes into ½-inch cubes. Place in a medium pot with enough salted water to cover by 1 inch. Bring to a boil and cook until tender, about 15 minutes. Meanwhile, trim and thinly slice scallions, separating greens and whites. Once potatoes are done, reserve ¼ cup cooking water, then drain." />
                <outline text="While potatoes cook, halve tomatoes. Halve, peel, and thinly slice shallot. Halve zucchini lengthwise. Scoop out seeds with a spoon and discard, then slice crosswise into ½-inch-thick half-moons. Heat a large drizzle of olive oil in a large pan over medium-high heat. Add zucchini and season with salt and pepper. Cook until just softened, 3-5 minutes. Add tomatoes, shallot, and 1 TBSP butter to pan. Cook, tossing, until softened, 2-3 minutes. Transfer veggies to a large bowl, then wipe out pan. " />
                <outline text="Return pot to low heat and add 1 TBSP butter and scallion whites. Cook, tossing, until softened, 1-2 minutes. Return potatoes to pot and mash until smooth, adding reserved water as needed to loosen. Stir in cheese, then season with plenty of salt and pepper. Keep over low heat until meal is ready" />
                <outline text="Heat a drizzle of olive oil in same pan over medium-high heat. Remove chicken from marinade, shaking of excess moisture. Season all over with salt, pepper, and remaining Italian seasoning. Add to pan and cook until no longer pink, 3-5 minutes per side. Remove from pan and let rest on a plate for about 3 minutes. Wipe out pan, return to medium-high heat, and stir in ¼ cup water and stock concentrate." />
                <outline text="Stir 1 TBSP butter and a squeeze or two of lemon into pan. Simmer until reduced, 2-4 minutes. Season with salt and pepper. Stir in any juices released by chicken. Stir half the scallion greens into potatoes in pot, then divide between plates along with veggies and chicken. Spoon sauce over everything. Garnish with remaining scallion greens." />
              </outline>
              <outline text="" />
              <outline text="Source">
                <outline text="HelloFresh" _note="&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.hellofresh.com/recipes/so-delizioso-chicken-cutlets-5c47801ac445fa5edd3985c2&quot;&gt;https://www.hellofresh.com/recipes/so-delizioso-chicken-cutlets-5c47801ac445fa5edd3985c2&lt;/a&gt;" />
              </outline>
              <outline text="0 Backlink" />
            </outline>
            <outline text="Lemon Garlic Chicken ">
              <outline text="&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.hellofresh.com/recipes/lemon-garlic-chicken-green-beans-63d947601010470fff073ac2&quot;&gt;https://www.hellofresh.com/recipes/lemon-garlic-chicken-green-beans-63d947601010470fff073ac2&lt;/a&gt;" />
            </outline>
            <outline text="Frijoles Fresca Bowls" _note="with Scallion Rice &amp; Pepper Jack&#10;">
              <outline text="Ingredients">
                <outline text="2 Scallions" />
                <outline text="Jasmine Rice" _note="¾ cup " />
                <outline text="1 Poblano Pepper" />
                <outline text="Black Beans" _note="13.4 ounce " />
                <outline text="1 Roma Tomato" />
                <outline text="Sour Cream" _note="4 tablespoon " />
                <outline text="Southwest Spice Blend" _note="1 tablespoon ">
                  <outline text="Cuman &amp; Tajin?" />
                </outline>
                <outline text="Green Salsa" _note="7.06 ounce ">
                  <outline text="Tomatillo Chile Salsa #Sprouts " />
                </outline>
                <outline text="Pepper Jack Cheese" _note="½ cup " />
                <outline text="+ lime?!" />
                <outline text="Also">
                  <outline text="1 tablespoonOlive Oil" />
                  <outline text="1 teaspoon Vegetable Oil" />
                  <outline text="½ teaspoon Sugar" />
                  <outline text="2 tablespoon Butter" />
                  <outline text="Salt" />
                  <outline text="Pepper" />
                </outline>
              </outline>
              <outline text="Directions">
                <outline text="&lt;b&gt;Wash and dry all produce.&lt;/b&gt;">
                  <outline text="Trim and thinly slice &lt;b&gt;&lt;mark class=&quot;colored c-sky&quot;&gt;2 scallions&lt;/mark&gt;&lt;/b&gt;, separating whites from greens." />
                  <outline text="Heat a drizzle of &lt;b&gt;&lt;mark class=&quot;colored c-sky&quot;&gt;oil &lt;/mark&gt;&lt;/b&gt;in a &lt;mark class=&quot;colored c-green&quot;&gt;small pot&lt;/mark&gt; over medium-high heat. " />
                  <outline text="Add scallion whites and cook until softened, 1 minute." />
                  <outline text="Stir in &lt;mark class=&quot;colored c-sky&quot;&gt;¾ cup of &lt;b&gt;rice &lt;/b&gt;&lt;/mark&gt;and &lt;mark class=&quot;colored c-sky&quot;&gt;1¼ cups &lt;b&gt;water&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/mark&gt;." _note="(2 ¼ cups for 4 servings)" />
                  <outline text="Bring to a boil, then cover and reduce to a low simmer. " />
                  <outline text="Cook until rice is tender, 15-18 minutes." />
                  <outline text="Keep covered off heat until ready to serve." />
                </outline>
                <outline text="&lt;b&gt;Prep &amp; Make Salsa Fresca&lt;/b&gt;">
                  <outline text="While rice cooks, core, deseed, and dice &lt;b&gt;&lt;mark class=&quot;colored c-sky&quot;&gt;poblano &lt;/mark&gt;&lt;/b&gt;into ½-inch pieces. ">
                    <outline text="Cut from the tip, as there are less seeds on that side." />
                  </outline>
                  <outline text="Drain and rinse a &lt;mark class=&quot;colored c-sky&quot;&gt;can of black &lt;b&gt;beans&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/mark&gt;. " />
                  <outline text="Finely dice a &lt;mark class=&quot;colored c-sky&quot;&gt;roma &lt;b&gt;tomato&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/mark&gt;" />
                  <outline text="In a &lt;mark class=&quot;colored c-green&quot;&gt;small bowl&lt;/mark&gt;, combine tomato, half the scallion greens, and a large drizzle of olive oil. Season generously with salt and pepper." />
                </outline>
                <outline text="&lt;b&gt;Make Crema&lt;/b&gt;">
                  <outline text="In a &lt;mark class=&quot;colored c-green&quot;&gt;second small bowl&lt;/mark&gt;, combine &lt;b&gt;&lt;mark class=&quot;colored c-sky&quot;&gt;sour cream&lt;/mark&gt;&lt;/b&gt; with ½ tsp &lt;mark class=&quot;colored c-sky&quot;&gt;Southwest Spice&lt;/mark&gt;. (You’ll use the remaining Southwest Spice later.) " _note=" (1 tsp for 4 servings)">
                    <outline text="Cumin and a little Tajin" />
                  </outline>
                  <outline text="Add water 1 tsp at a time until mixture reaches a drizzling consistency." />
                </outline>
                <outline text="&lt;b&gt;Cook Poblano&lt;/b&gt;">
                  <outline text="Heat a drizzle of olive oil in a&lt;mark class=&quot;colored c-green&quot;&gt; large pan&lt;/mark&gt; over medium-high heat. " />
                  <outline text="Add poblano and cook, stirring occasionally, until softened and lightly browned, 4-5 minutes. Season with salt and pepper." />
                  <outline text="Reduce heat to medium." />
                </outline>
                <outline text="&lt;b&gt;Cook Beans&lt;/b&gt;">
                  <outline text="Stir beans, remaining Southwest Spice, and 1 TBSP &lt;b&gt;&lt;mark class=&quot;colored c-sky&quot;&gt;butter &lt;/mark&gt;&lt;/b&gt;into pan with poblano. " _note="(2 TBSP for 4 servings)" />
                  <outline text="Cook, stirring, until mixture is fragrant and butter has melted, 1-2 minutes." />
                  <outline text="Stir in &lt;b&gt;&lt;mark class=&quot;colored c-sky&quot;&gt;green salsa&lt;/mark&gt;&lt;/b&gt; (7 oz) and ½ tsp &lt;b&gt;&lt;mark class=&quot;colored c-sky&quot;&gt;sugar&lt;/mark&gt;&lt;/b&gt; (1 tsp for 4). " />
                  <outline text="Cook, stirring occasionally, until beans are softened, 1-3 minutes. " />
                  <outline text="Season with salt and pepper. " />
                  <outline text="Turn off heat." />
                </outline>
                <outline text="&lt;b&gt;Finish &amp; Serve&lt;/b&gt;">
                  <outline text="Fluff rice with a fork; stir in 1 TBSP &lt;b&gt;&lt;mark class=&quot;colored c-sky&quot;&gt;butter &lt;/mark&gt;&lt;/b&gt;until melted." />
                  <outline text="Divide rice between &lt;mark class=&quot;colored c-green&quot;&gt;bowls &lt;/mark&gt;and top with bean mixture, &lt;mark class=&quot;colored c-sky&quot;&gt;pepper jack &lt;b&gt;cheese&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/mark&gt;, salsa fresca, and crema. " />
                  <outline text="Garnish with remaining scallion greens and &lt;b&gt;&lt;mark class=&quot;colored c-sky&quot;&gt;lime&lt;/mark&gt;&lt;/b&gt;, then serve." />
                </outline>
              </outline>
              <outline text="Source">
                <outline text="HelloFresh &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.hellofresh.com/recipes/frijoles-fresca-bowls-602c3804c0de180f8b75f8cd&quot;&gt;Web&lt;/a&gt;" />
              </outline>
              <outline text="#vegetarian #easy #mexican " />
              <outline text="0 Backlink" />
            </outline>
            <outline text="Goulash">
              <outline text="Ingredients">
                <outline text="ground beef" _note="2 lbs ">
                  <outline text="For a healthier version of this comforting meal, replace the beef with ground turkey or chicken." />
                  <outline text="Try replacing the ground meat (or a portion of it) with ground pork for an added kick of flavor." />
                </outline>
                <outline text="1 yellow onion" _note="chopped" />
                <outline text="3 cloves garlic" _note="minced" />
                <outline text="canned diced tomatoes" _note="30 oz, undrained" />
                <outline text="tomato sauce" _note="30 oz " />
                <outline text="water" _note="3 cups" />
                <outline text="Worcestershire sauce" _note="2 tbsp " />
                <outline text="Italian seasoning" _note="1 tbsp " />
                <outline text="seasoned salt" _note="2 tsp ">
                  <outline text="The seasoned salt in the recipe might seem odd, but don’t skip it! It adds the perfect amount of seasoning. When I’ve skipped this ingredient in the past, I’ve noticed a difference in overall flavor of the dish." />
                </outline>
                <outline text="elbow macaroni" _note="16 oz " />
              </outline>
              <outline text="Directions">
                <outline text="In a Dutch oven or large saucepan, cook ground beef over medium heat until no longer pink. Drain grease. Add onion and garlic and cook for 3 minutes, or until soft and fragrant.">
                  <outline text="Add 2 bay leaves and/or a splash of red wine to the pot before cooking for extra flavor." />
                </outline>
                <outline text="Add diced tomatoes, tomato sauce, water, Worcestershire sauce, Italian seasoning, seasoned salt and elbow macaroni to the pan. Mix well and bring to a boil. ">
                  <outline text="Replace all or a portion of the water in the recipe with LOW SODIUM beef broth for an even more flavorful meal." />
                  <outline text="Add a chopped green bell pepper to the onion mixture for added texture and flavor. Red, yellow, orange or green peppers would all taste great." />
                  <outline text="I recently had a friend tell me that she added 1 tablespoon of soy sauce to this recipe and that it was super yummy." />
                </outline>
                <outline text="Reduce to medium-low heat, cover pan and simmer for 25-30 minutes or until pasta is cooked through.">
                  <outline text="Sprinkle shredded cheddar cheese or Parmesan over the top just before serving for an extra cheesy version of this dish." />
                </outline>
                <outline text="Remove from heat and serve immediately!" />
              </outline>
              <outline text="Source">
                <outline text="&lt;a href=&quot;https://pipandebby.com/pip-ebby/best-ever-goulash/&quot;&gt;https://pipandebby.com/pip-ebby/best-ever-goulash/&lt;/a&gt;" />
              </outline>
              <outline text="#lasts_multiple_days " />
            </outline>
            <outline text="Southwest Stuffed Zucchini Boats " _note="with Pico de Gallo, Avocado Crema &amp; Cilantro&#10;">
              <outline text="Ingredients " _note="2 Servings">
                <outline text="1 Red Onion" />
                <outline text="2 Zucchini" />
                <outline text="Jasmine Rice" _note="¾ cup" />
                <outline text="+ Can of Black Beans" />
                <outline text="Southwest Spice Blend" _note="1 tablespoon" />
                <outline text="Veggie Stock Concentrate " />
                <outline text="1 Roma Tomato" />
                <outline text="1 Lime" />
                <outline text="Cilantro" _note="¼ ounce" />
                <outline text="Guacamole" _note="4 tablespoon" />
                <outline text="Sour Cream" _note="4 tablespoon" />
                <outline text="Hot Sauce" _note="1 teaspoon" />
                <outline text="Pepper Jack Cheese (or Monterey Jack)" _note="½ cup" />
                <outline text="Also">
                  <outline text="Olive Oil" _note="2 teaspoon" />
                  <outline text="Butter" _note="1 tablespoon" />
                  <outline text="Salt" />
                  <outline text="Pepper" />
                </outline>
              </outline>
              <outline text="Directions">
                <outline text="Prep">
                  <outline text="Adjust rack to top position and preheat oven to 450 degrees. Wash and dry all produce." />
                  <outline text="Halve, peel, and finely dice &lt;b&gt;&lt;mark class=&quot;colored c-green&quot;&gt;onion&lt;/mark&gt;&lt;/b&gt;." />
                  <outline text="Trim and halve &lt;b&gt;&lt;mark class=&quot;colored c-green&quot;&gt;zucchini&lt;/mark&gt;&lt;/b&gt; lengthwise; scoop out seeds with a spoon and discard." />
                  <outline text="Open and drain black beans" />
                </outline>
                <outline text="Cook Rice">
                  <outline text="Heat 1 TBSP &lt;b&gt;&lt;mark class=&quot;colored c-green&quot;&gt;butter&lt;/mark&gt;&lt;/b&gt; (2 TBSP for 4&amp;nbsp;servings) and a drizzle of &lt;mark class=&quot;colored c-green&quot;&gt;olive oil &lt;/mark&gt;in a &lt;b&gt;medium pot&lt;/b&gt; over medium-high heat. " />
                  <outline text="Add ¾ of the onion; season with &lt;mark class=&quot;colored c-green&quot;&gt;salt&lt;/mark&gt; and pepper. " />
                  <outline text="Cook, stirring, until softened, 4-5 minutes." />
                  <outline text="Add black beans." />
                  <outline text="Add 3/4 cup of rice and Southwest Spice; stir to coat." />
                  <outline text="Stir in stock concentrate, 1¼ cups water (2¼ cups for 4), and a big pinch of salt. " />
                  <outline text="Bring to a boil; cover and reduce to a low simmer. " />
                  <outline text="Cook until tender, 15-18 minutes." />
                  <outline text="Keep covered off heat until ready to use in step 5." />
                </outline>
                <outline text="Roast Zucchini ">
                  <outline text="While rice cooks, place zucchini on a baking sheet. " />
                  <outline text="Rub all over with a drizzle of olive oil. " />
                  <outline text="Season with salt and pepper, then arrange cut sides down." />
                  <outline text="Roast on top rack until browned and tender, 15-20 minutes." />
                </outline>
                <outline text="Make Pico &amp; Crema">
                  <outline text="Meanwhile, dice tomato. Roughly chop cilantro. Zest and halve lime." />
                  <outline text="In a small bowl, combine tomato, half the cilantro, a squeeze of lime juice to taste, and as much remaining onion as you like. Season with salt and pepper." />
                  <outline text="In a separate small bowl, combine guacamole, lime zest, and half the sour cream (save the rest for serving). Squeeze in lime juice to taste. Season with salt and pepper. Add water 1 tsp at a time until mixture reaches a drizzling consistency." />
                </outline>
                <outline text="Stuff &amp; Broil Zucchini ">
                  <outline text="Once zucchini is tender, remove baking sheet from oven. Heat broiler to high." />
                  <outline text="Fluff rice with a fork and season with salt and pepper." />
                  <outline text="Flip over zucchini and stuff with as much rice as will fit (there will be plenty left over). Evenly top with pepper jack." />
                  <outline text="Broil until cheese is melted and lightly browned, 2-3 minutes. TIP: Watch carefully to avoid burning." />
                </outline>
                <outline text="——————————" />
                <outline text="Serve">
                  <outline text="Divide remaining rice between plates and top with stuffed zucchini. Top with avocado crema, pico de gallo, remaining cilantro, and a dollop of remaining sour cream. Drizzle with hot sauce if desired and serve." />
                </outline>
              </outline>
              <outline text="Source">
                <outline text="HelloFresh: &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.hellofresh.com/recipes/southwest-stuffed-zucchini-boats-6006f81a1764635a612f2f02&quot;&gt;Web&lt;/a&gt; | &lt;a href=&quot;https://hellofresh.com/recipecards/card/southwest-stuffed-zucchini-boats-6006f81a1764635a612f2f02-92a07ec5.pdf&quot;&gt;PDF&lt;/a&gt;" />
              </outline>
              <outline text="1 Backlink" />
            </outline>
            <outline text="Spanish Chicken ">
              <outline text="Ingredients #needsattention ">
                <outline text="&lt;a href=&quot;https://pinchofyum.com/one-pot-spanish-chicken-potatoes&quot;&gt;https://pinchofyum.com/one-pot-spanish-chicken-potatoes&lt;/a&gt;" />
              </outline>
              <outline text="Directions" />
              <outline text="Source #needsattention " />
            </outline>
            <outline text="Chicken Stew with Biscuits" _note="on hand">
              <outline text="Ingredients">
                <outline text="For the Stew">
                  <outline text="3 whole (6 split) chicken breasts" _note="bone in, skin on&#10;" />
                  <outline text="olive oil" _note="3 tablespoons " />
                  <outline text="Kosher salt and freshly ground black pepper" />
                  <outline text="chicken stock" _note="5 cups, preferably homemade&#10;" />
                  <outline text="2 chicken bouillon cubes" />
                  <outline text="unsalted butter" _note="12 tablespoons (1 1/2 sticks) " />
                  <outline text="2 yellow onions" _note="2 cups chopped " />
                  <outline text="flour" _note="3/4 cup " />
                  <outline text="heavy cream" _note="1/4 cup " />
                  <outline text="4 carrots" _note="2 cups medium-diced, blanched for 2 minutes&#10;" />
                  <outline text="1 package frozen peas" _note="10-ounce (2 cups)&#10;" />
                  <outline text="frozen small whole onions" _note="1 1/2 cups " />
                  <outline text="fresh parsley" _note="1/2 cup minced " />
                </outline>
                <outline text="For the biscuits:">
                  <outline text="flour" _note="2 cups " />
                  <outline text="baking powder" _note="1 tablespoon " />
                  <outline text="kosher salt" _note="1 teaspoon " />
                  <outline text="sugar" _note="1 teaspoon " />
                  <outline text="unsalted butter" _note="1/4 pound (1 stick) cold, diced&#10;" />
                  <outline text="half-and-half" _note="3/4 cup " />
                  <outline text="fresh parsley" _note="1/2 cup chopped " />
                  <outline text="1 egg" _note="mixed with 1 tablespoon water, for egg wash" />
                </outline>
              </outline>
              <outline text="Directions" _note="1 Hour 15 Minutes&#10;" />
              <outline text="Source">
                <outline text="&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.foodnetwork.com/recipes/ina-garten/chicken-stew-with-biscuits-recipe-1941446&quot;&gt;https://www.foodnetwork.com/recipes/ina-garten/chicken-stew-with-biscuits-recipe-1941446&lt;/a&gt;" />
              </outline>
            </outline>
            <outline text="Chicken Shawarma">
              <outline text="Ingredients ">
                <outline text="chicken thigh fillets, skinless and boneless" _note="1 kg / 2 lb ">
                  <outline text="I feel strongly that this is best made with thigh because it’s got more fat so you get beautiful caramelisation. But it’s still super tasty made with chicken breast. The best way is to cut them in half horizontally to make 2 thin steaks no thicker than 1 cm/ 2/5″ each. If needed, pound lightly. Marinate per recipe. Then cook on a high heat (not medium high per recipe) for just 2 minutes on each side until golden. They will be juicy and beautiful inside!" />
                </outline>
                <outline text="&lt;b&gt;&lt;mark class=&quot;colored c-teal&quot;&gt;MARINADE&lt;/mark&gt;&lt;/b&gt;">
                  <outline text="garlic clove" _note="1 large, minced (or 2 small cloves)&#10;" />
                  <outline text="ground coriander" _note="1 tbsp " />
                  <outline text="ground cumin" _note="1 tbsp " />
                  <outline text="ground cardamon" _note="1 tbsp" />
                  <outline text="ground cayenne pepper " _note="1 tsp (reduce to 1/2 tsp to make it not spicy)&#10;" />
                  <outline text="smoked paprika" _note="2 tsp " />
                  <outline text="salt" _note="2 tsp " />
                  <outline text="Black pepper" />
                  <outline text="lemon juice" _note="2 tbsp" />
                  <outline text="olive oil" _note="3 tbsp" />
                </outline>
                <outline text="&lt;b&gt;&lt;mark class=&quot;colored c-teal&quot;&gt;YOGHURT SAUCE&lt;/mark&gt;&lt;/b&gt;">
                  <outline text="Greek yogurt" _note="1 cup " />
                  <outline text="garlic , crushed" _note="1 clove " />
                  <outline text="cumin" _note="1 tsp " />
                  <outline text="lemon juice" _note="Squeeze of " />
                  <outline text="Salt and pepper" />
                </outline>
                <outline text="&lt;b&gt;&lt;mark class=&quot;colored c-teal&quot;&gt;TO SERVE&lt;/mark&gt;&lt;/b&gt;">
                  <outline text="4 – 5 flatbreads" _note="(Lebanese or pita bread orhomemade soft flatbreads)" />
                  <outline text="Sliced lettuce" _note=" (cos or iceberg)" />
                  <outline text="Tomato slices" />
                  <outline text="Red onion" _note=" finely sliced&#10;" />
                  <outline text="Cheese" _note="shredded (optional)" />
                  <outline text="Hot sauce of choice" _note="(optional)" />
                </outline>
              </outline>
              <outline text="Directions ">
                <outline text="1. Marinade chicken">
                  <outline text="Combine the marinade ingredients in a large ziplock bag.">
                    <outline text="&lt;b&gt;&lt;mark class=&quot;colored c-teal&quot;&gt;MARINADE&lt;/mark&gt;&lt;/b&gt;" />
                  </outline>
                  <outline text="Add the chicken, seal it, then massage it (from the outside) with your hands to make sure each piece is coated. " />
                  <outline text="Marinate 24 hours (minimum 3 hours)." />
                </outline>
                <outline text="2. Yogurt Sauce">
                  <outline text="Combine the Yogurt Sauce ingredients in a bowl and mix. ">
                    <outline text="&lt;b&gt;&lt;mark class=&quot;colored c-teal&quot;&gt;YOGHURT SAUCE&lt;/mark&gt;&lt;/b&gt;" />
                  </outline>
                  <outline text="Cover and put in the fridge until required (it will last for 3 days in the fridge)." />
                </outline>
                <outline text="3. Preheat stove (or BBQ)">
                  <outline text="Heat a large non-stick skillet with 1 tablespoon over medium-high heat." _note=" or lightly brush a BBQ hotplate/grills with oil and heat to medium high.">
                    <outline text="&lt;i&gt;Cooking on a BBQ or stove is best to get the caramelisation. Baking doesn’t yield quite the same flavour – but still very good! Bake at 425F/220C for 20 – 25 minutes until a browned.&lt;/i&gt;" />
                  </outline>
                </outline>
                <outline text="4. Cook chicken">
                  <outline text="Place chicken in the skillet or on the grill and cook the first side for 4 to 5 minutes until nicely charred. " />
                  <outline text="Turn and cook the other side for 3 to 4 minutes." _note="The 2nd side takes less time.&#10;" />
                  <outline text="Meanwhile, slice tomatoes 🍅 and lettuce 🥬 " />
                  <outline text="Cut onions" />
                </outline>
                <outline text="5. Rest">
                  <outline text="Remove chicken from the grill and cover loosely with foil. " />
                  <outline text="Set aside to rest for 5 minutes." />
                </outline>
                <outline text="&lt;b&gt;&lt;mark class=&quot;colored c-teal&quot;&gt;TO SERVE&lt;/mark&gt;&lt;/b&gt;" />
                <outline text="Slice chicken and pile onto platter alongside flatbreads, salad (lettuce, tomato, onion) and the Yoghurt Sauce">
                  <outline text=" (or dairy-free Tahini sauce from &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.recipetineats.com/roasted-broccolini-with-tahini-sauce-ottolenghi-recipe/&quot;&gt;this recipe&lt;/a&gt;)." />
                </outline>
                <outline text="To make a wrap, get a piece of flatbread and smear with Yoghurt Sauce. Top with a bit of lettuce and tomato and Chicken Shawarma. Roll up and enjoy!" />
                <outline text="" _note="&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=fYzUDT2phtQ&quot;&gt;https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=fYzUDT2phtQ&lt;/a&gt;" />
              </outline>
              <outline text="" />
              <outline text="Source" _note="&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.recipetineats.com/chicken-sharwama-middle-eastern/#wprm-recipe-container-22007&quot;&gt;https://www.recipetineats.com/chicken-sharwama-middle-eastern/#wprm-recipe-container-22007&lt;/a&gt;&#10;">
                <outline text="Video: &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=fYzUDT2phtQ&quot;&gt;https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=fYzUDT2phtQ&lt;/a&gt;" />
              </outline>
            </outline>
            <outline text="Chicken &amp; Dumplings">
              <outline text="Ingredients #needsattention " />
              <outline text="Directions #needsattention " />
              <outline text="Source" />
            </outline>
            <outline text="Figgy Balsamic Pork" _note="with Roasted Green Beans and Rosemary Potatoes">
              <outline text="Ingredients">
                <outline text="Shallot #Sprouts " />
                <outline text="Rosemary #Sprouts ">
                  <outline text="Rosemary has a distinctively piney herb flavor that can taste strong. You may want to use just a pinch or two of it at first, then add more to taste." />
                </outline>
                <outline text="Yukon Gold Potatoes #Sprouts " />
                <outline text="Pork Tenderloin" />
                <outline text="Green Beans" />
                <outline text="Chicken Stock Concentrate" />
                <outline text="Balsamic Vinegar" />
                <outline text="Fig Jam" />
                <outline text="Also...">
                  <outline text="2 Baking Sheets" />
                  <outline text="Large Pan" />
                  <outline text="4 tsp Olive Oil" />
                  <outline text="1 tbsp Butter" />
                </outline>
              </outline>
              <outline text="Directions">
                <outline text="Prep">
                  <outline text="Adjust racks to top and middle positions and preheat oven to 450 degrees. " />
                  <outline text="Wash and dry all produce. " />
                  <outline text="Halve, peel, and finely chop &lt;b&gt;shallot&lt;/b&gt;. " />
                  <outline text="Strip and finely chop enough &lt;b&gt;rosemary&lt;/b&gt; leaves from stems to give you 2 tsp (4 tsp for 4 servings). " />
                  <outline text="Dice &lt;b&gt;potatoes&lt;/b&gt; into ½-inch pieces." />
                </outline>
                <outline text="Roast Potatoes">
                  <outline text="Toss &lt;b&gt;potatoes&lt;/b&gt; on a baking sheet with a drizzle of &lt;b&gt;olive oil&lt;/b&gt;, half the &lt;b&gt;rosemary&lt;/b&gt;, and a pinch of &lt;b&gt;salt&lt;/b&gt; and &lt;b&gt;pepper&lt;/b&gt;. " />
                  <outline text="Roast on top rack, tossing halfway through, until tender and crisped, 20-25 minutes." />
                </outline>
                <outline text="Sear Pork">
                  <outline text="Meanwhile, pat &lt;b&gt;pork&lt;/b&gt; dry with paper towels; season all over with &lt;b&gt;salt&lt;/b&gt; and &lt;b&gt;pepper&lt;/b&gt;. " />
                  <outline text="Heat a drizzle of &lt;b&gt;olive oil &lt;/b&gt;in a large pan over medium heat. " />
                  <outline text="Add pork and sear, turning occasionally, until browned all over, 4-8 minutes. " />
                  <outline text="Transfer to a second baking sheet." />
                </outline>
                <outline text="Roast Green Beans and Pork">
                  <outline text="Toss &lt;b&gt;green beans&lt;/b&gt; with a drizzle of &lt;b&gt;olive oil &lt;/b&gt;and a pinch of &lt;b&gt;salt&lt;/b&gt; and &lt;b&gt;pepper&lt;/b&gt; on same sheet with &lt;b&gt;pork&lt;/b&gt;. " />
                  <outline text="Roast on middle rack until pork is cooked through and green beans are tender, 10-12 minutes. " />
                  <outline text="Let pork rest a few minutes after removing from oven, then cut into thin slices." />
                </outline>
                <outline text="Make Pan Sauce">
                  <outline text="Heat a drizzle of &lt;b&gt;olive oil&lt;/b&gt; in pan used for pork over medium heat." />
                  <outline text="Add &lt;b&gt;shallot&lt;/b&gt; and remaining chopped &lt;b&gt;rosemary&lt;/b&gt;." />
                  <outline text="Cook, stirring, until softened, about 1 minute." />
                  <outline text="Stir in &lt;b&gt;stock concentrate&lt;/b&gt;, &lt;b&gt;vinegar&lt;/b&gt;, 1 TBSP &lt;b&gt;jam&lt;/b&gt; , and ¼ cup &lt;b&gt;water.&lt;/b&gt;" _note="(2 TBSP of jam for 4 servings, ½ cup water for 4 servings)" />
                  <outline text="Simmer until thick and saucy, 2-3 minutes. " />
                  <outline text="Remove pan from heat and stir in 1 TBSP &lt;b&gt;butter&lt;/b&gt; until melted. Season with &lt;b&gt;salt&lt;/b&gt; and &lt;b&gt;pepper&lt;/b&gt;." />
                </outline>
                <outline text="Plate and Serve">
                  <outline text="Divide potatoes, green beans, and pork between plates. Drizzle&lt;b&gt; pan sauce&lt;/b&gt; over pork and serve." />
                </outline>
              </outline>
              <outline text="Source: HelloFresh &lt;a href=&quot;https://ddw4dkk7s1lkt.cloudfront.net/card/figgy-balsamic-pork-5ca4f2c1c445fa462a671182-3b3c17b4.pdf&quot;&gt;PDF&lt;/a&gt;" />
              <outline text="#kyles_favorite #pork" />
            </outline>
            <outline text="Meatloaf">
              <outline text="Ingredients #needsattention ">
                <outline text="Worcestershire sauce" />
                <outline text="A1 Sauce" />
                <outline text="Ground Beef" _note="1 lb&#10;" />
                <outline text="Beef Bone Broth Concentrate" />
              </outline>
              <outline text="Directions" />
              <outline text="#beef" />
            </outline>
            <outline text="Lasagna Bolognese Simplified">
              <outline text="&lt;i&gt;Note that some no-boil lasagna noodle packages contain only 12 noodles; this recipe requires 15 noodles. For assembly, both the meat sauce and the béchamel should be just warm to the touch, not piping hot.&lt;/i&gt;" />
              <outline text="Ingredients">
                <outline text="Meat Sauce">
                  <outline text="1 carrot, peeled and chopped coarse " />
                  <outline text="1 celery rib, chopped coarse" />
                  <outline text="1/2 cup coarsely chopped onion" />
                  <outline text="1 (28-ounce) can whole peeled tomatoes" />
                  <outline text="2 tablespoons unsalted butter" />
                  <outline text="8 ounces 90 percent lean ground beef" />
                  <outline text="8 ounces ground pork" />
                  <outline text="8 ounces ground veal" />
                  <outline text="1½ cups whole milk" />
                  <outline text="1½ cups dry white wine" />
                  <outline text="2 tablespoons tomato paste" />
                  <outline text="1 teaspoon salt" />
                  <outline text="3/4 teaspoon pepper" />
                </outline>
                <outline text="Béchamel">
                  <outline text="4 tablespoons unsalted butter " />
                  <outline text="1/4 cup all-purpose flour" />
                  <outline text="4 cups whole milk" />
                  <outline text="3/4 teaspoon salt" />
                  <outline text="15 no-boil lasagna noodles" />
                  <outline text="4 ounces Parmesan cheese, grated (2 cups)" />
                </outline>
              </outline>
              <outline text="Directions">
                <outline text="&lt;b&gt;1. FOR THE MEAT SAUCE&lt;/b&gt;: ">
                  <outline text="Pulse carrot, cel- ery, and onion in food processor until finely chopped, about 10 pulses, scraping down sides of bowl as needed; transfer to bowl. Pulse tomatoes and their juice in now-empty processor until finely chopped, 6 to 8 pulses." />
                </outline>
                <outline text="2. Continue">
                  <outline text="Melt butter in Dutch oven over medium heat. Add chopped vegetable mixture and cook, stirring occasionally, until softened, about 5 minutes. Stir in beef, pork, and veal and cook, breaking 1-inch pieces with wooden spoon, for 1 minute. Stir in milk and bring to simmer, breaking meat into meat into 1/2-inch pieces. Continue to cook, stirring often to break up meat into small pieces, until most of liquid has evaporated, 18 to 20 minutes longer. Add wine, bring to simmer, and cook, stirring occasionally, until liquid has evaporated, 20 to 30 minutes. Stir in tomato paste and cook until combined, about 1 minute. Stir in tomatoes and their juice, salt, and pepper, bring to simmer; and cook until sauce is slightly thickened and measures 6 cups, about 15 minutes. Transfer meat sauce to bowl and set aside to cool, about 30 minutes. (Cooled meat sauce can be refrigerated for up to 2 days; gently reheat before assembling lasagna.)" />
                </outline>
                <outline text="&lt;b&gt;  3. For the Béchamel:&lt;/b&gt; ">
                  <outline text="While meat sauce simmers, melt butter in medium saucepan over medium heat. Add flour and cook, stirring constantly, until thoroughly combined, about 1½ minutes; mixture should not brown. Gradually whisk in milk; increase heat to medium-high and bring to boil, whisking frequently. Add salt, reduce heat to medium-low, and simmer until sauce thickens and measures 3 1/2 cups, about 10 minutes, stirring occasionally and making sure to scrape bottom and corners of saucepan. Transfer béchamel to second bowl and set aside to cool, about 30 minutes. (Cooled béchamel can be refrigerated for up to 2 days; gently reheat before assembling lasagna.)" />
                </outline>
                <outline text="4. If using ready to bake nooodles">
                  <outline text="Adjust oven rack to middle position and heat oven to 425 degrees. Pour 2 inches boiling water into 13 by 9-inch baking dish. Slip noodles into water, one at a time, and soak until pliable, about 5 minutes, separating noodles with tip of sharp knife to prevent sticking. Remove noodles from water and place in single layer on clean dish tow els; discard water. Dry dish and spray lightly with vegetable oil spray." />
                </outline>
                <outline text="  5.Combine ">
                  <outline text="Stir warm béchamel to recombine, then stir 3/4 cup béchamel into warm meat sauce until thoroughly combined. Spread 1 cup béchamel-enriched meat sauce evenly over bottom of prepared dish. Arrange 3 noodles in single layer on top of sauce. Spoon 1 1/4 cups béchamel-enriched meat sauce over noodles, spreading sauce to edge of noodles but not to edge of dish. Drizzle 1/3 cup béchamel evenly over meat sauce and sprinkle with 1/3 cup Parmesan. Repeat layering of noodles, béchamel-enriched meat sauce, béchamel, and Parmesan 3 more times. For final layer, arrange remaining 3 noodles on top and cover completely with remaining béchamel. Sprinkle with remaining 2/3 cup Parmesan." />
                </outline>
                <outline text="6. Bake">
                  <outline text="Cover dish tightly with aluminum foil that has been sprayed with oil spray and bake until edges are just bubbling, about 30 minutes, rotating dish halfway through baking. Remove foil, increase oven temperature to 450 degrees, and continue to bake until cheese on top becomes spotty brown, about 15 minutes longer. Let lasagna cool for 15 minutes before serving." />
                </outline>
              </outline>
              <outline text="Source">
                <outline text="Cook’s Illustrated Comfort Food Favorites 2019" />
              </outline>
              <outline text="  " />
              <outline text="Servings: 10" />
            </outline>
            <outline text="Southwest Tilapia" _note="with Charred Corn Salad and Buttery Lime Rice">
              <outline text="#low_calorie " />
              <outline text="&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.hellofresh.com/recipes/2019-w31-r13-southwest-tilapia-5d07cf27cb6dea00126134fe&quot;&gt;https://www.hellofresh.com/recipes/2019-w31-r13-southwest-tilapia-5d07cf27cb6dea00126134fe&lt;/a&gt;" />
            </outline>
            <outline text="One Skillet Savory Beef Tips and Gravy">
              <outline text="Ingredients">
                <outline text="butter" _note="3 tablespoons " />
                <outline text="crimini mushrooms" _note="1/2 lb sliced " />
                <outline text="onion" _note="1/2 cup finely chopped " />
                <outline text="2 large cloves garlic" _note="minced" />
                <outline text="beef tenderloin" _note="1 lb or good quality beef steak ( I use petite shoulder) cut in bite size strips" />
                <outline text="flour" _note="1/4 cup" />
                <outline text="salt" _note="1/4 teaspoon " />
                <outline text="fresh ground pepper" _note="1/4 teaspoon " />
                <outline text="olive oil" _note="2 tablespoon " />
                <outline text="red wine" _note="1/4 cup good quality " />
                <outline text="low sodium beef broth" _note="1 can (14 ounce)&#10;" />
                <outline text="Worcestershire Sauce" _note="2 tablespoons " />
                <outline text="flour " _note="1/4 cup (Wondra flour recommended)&#10;" />
                <outline text="Salt &amp; Pepper to taste" />
              </outline>
              <outline text="Directions">
                <outline text="Add butter to large skillet over medium high heat. When melted toss in mushrooms and cook until light golden brown; approximately 8 minutes. Add onions and continue cooking for 2-3 minutes or until onions start to soften and mushrooms turn golden brown. Reduce heat to low and add garlic; cook for 30 seconds. Remove from pan and plate." />
                <outline text="In large ziploc bag add flour, steak bites, salt and pepper. Shake to coat. Add olive oil to skillet over medium high heat. Add steak and cook just until browned. Remove to plate." />
                <outline text="Add red wine to skillet and deglaze the pan; scraping up the brown bits from the bottom. Pour 1/2 cup of beef broth in bowl and set aside. Add REMAINING beef broth and Worcestershire Sauce. Simmer for 5 minutes; stirring a couple of times." />
                <outline text="In small bowl whisk together beef broth and 1/4 cup flour. Whisk flour mixture into skillet with beef broth mixture. Cook until slightly thickened; approximately 2 minutes. Add mushroom mixture and beef back to pan; simmer for 15 minutes. Salt &amp; pepper to taste. Serve over egg noodles, rice or mashed potatoes." />
              </outline>
              <outline text="Source">
                <outline text="&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.smalltownwoman.com/one-skillet-savory-beef-tips-and-gravy/&quot;&gt;https://www.smalltownwoman.com/one-skillet-savory-beef-tips-and-gravy/&lt;/a&gt;" />
              </outline>
            </outline>
          </outline>
          <outline text="&lt;b&gt;Let's Eat This Soon 👍&lt;/b&gt;">
            <outline text="Mexican Lasagna ">
              <outline text="Ingredients ">
                <outline text="Turmeric Rice with black Beans" />
                <outline text="Beef" />
                <outline text="Red onion" />
                <outline text="Garlic" />
                <outline text="Cumin" />
                <outline text="Tomatoes" />
                <outline text="Corn" />
                <outline text="Layer with: Tortillas, Cheese, and Taco Bell’s Avocado Ranch sauce " />
                <outline text="Fits well in a bread pan" />
              </outline>
              <outline text="#kyles_favorite " />
            </outline>
            <outline text="Amazing Apricot Chicken" _note="with Jasmine Rice &amp; Green Beans&#10;">
              <outline text="Ingredients" _note="2 Servings">
                <outline text="1 unit Shallot" />
                <outline text="½ cup Jasmine Rice" />
                <outline text="6 ounce Green Beans" />
                <outline text="10 ounce Chicken Cutlets" />
                <outline text="¼ ounce Thyme" />
                <outline text="2 tablespoon Apricot Jam" />
                <outline text="5 teaspoon Balsamic Vinegar" />
                <outline text="1 unit Chicken Stock Concentrate" />
                <outline text="Also">
                  <outline text="2 teaspoon Olive Oil" />
                  <outline text="1 tablespoon Butter" />
                  <outline text="Salt" />
                  <outline text="Pepper" />
                  <outline text="1 teaspoon Vegetable Oil" />
                </outline>
              </outline>
              <outline text="Directions">
                <outline text="Prep Shallot">
                  <outline text="Adjust rack to top position and preheat oven to 425 degrees. Wash and dry all produce. Halve, peel, and mince half the shallot (save the rest for another use; for 4 servings, mince whole shallot)." />
                </outline>
                <outline text="Cook Rice">
                  <outline text="In a small pot, combine rice, ¾ cup water (1½ cups for 4 servings), and a big pinch of salt. Bring to a boil, then cover and reduce to a low simmer. Cook until rice is tender, 15-18 minutes. Keep covered off heat until ready to serve." />
                </outline>
                <outline text="Roast Green Beans">
                  <outline text="While rice cooks, toss green beans on a baking sheet with a drizzle of oil, salt, and pepper. Roast on top rack until browned and tender, 12-15 minutes." />
                </outline>
                <outline text="Cook Chicken">
                  <outline text="Meanwhile, pat chicken dry with paper towels; season all over with salt and pepper. Heat a drizzle of olive oil in a large pan over medium-high heat. Add chicken and cook until browned and cooked through, 3-5 minutes per side. Turn off heat; transfer chicken to a cutting board and set aside to rest. Wipe out pan." />
                </outline>
                <outline text="Make Sauce">
                  <outline text="Add shallot, thyme sprigs, and a drizzle of olive oil to same pan over medium heat. Cook, stirring, until shallot is softened, 1-2 minutes. Stir in jam and 1 TBSP vinegar (use all the vinegar for 4 servings). Let simmer until syrupy, 1-2 minutes. Stir in stock concentrate and ¼ cup water (⅓ cup for 4). Simmer until thickened, 1-2 minutes. Turn off heat; stir in 1 TBSP butter (2 TBSP for 4) until melted. TIP: Stir in a splash of water if sauce seems thick." />
                </outline>
                <outline text="Finish and Serve">
                  <outline text="Remove thyme sprigs from pan and discard. Season sauce with salt and pepper. Fluff rice with a fork; season with salt and pepper. Thinly slice chicken; divide between plates with rice and green beans. Drizzle chicken with sauce and serve." />
                </outline>
              </outline>
              <outline text="Source: &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.hellofresh.com/recipes/amazing-apricot-chicken-5e5ea6149072d614f4787927&quot;&gt;HelloFresh&lt;/a&gt; | &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.hellofresh.com/recipecards/card/amazing-apricot-chicken-5e5ea6149072d614f4787927-f4869797.pdf?_gl=1*z7nuao*_ga*MTkyNzQwNjU3Mi4xNzA1NjI0OTMw*_ga_6XTFRPBHKQ*MTcwNTYyNDkyOS4xLjEuMTcwNTYyNTM2OS4wLjAuMA&quot;&gt;PDF&lt;/a&gt;" />
              <outline text="" />
            </outline>
            <outline text="Smoky Black Bean and Corn Tostadas" _note="with Pico de Gallo and Lime Crema">
              <outline text="Ingredients">
                <outline text="Roma Tomato" _note="#Sprouts " />
                <outline text="Jalapeño" _note="#Sprouts " />
                <outline text="Yellow Onion" _note="#Sprouts " />
                <outline text="Sour Cream" _note="#ALDI " />
                <outline text="Corn" _note="13.4 oz" />
                <outline text="Flour Tortillas" _note="#ALDI " />
                <outline text="Cilantro" _note="#Sprouts&#10;" />
                <outline text="Lime" _note="#Sprouts " />
                <outline text="Black Beans" _note="13.4 oz #ALDI&#10;" />
                <outline text="Southwest Spice Blend" _note="Sub out for Cumin and Tajin&#10;" />
                <outline text="Mexican Cheese Blend - Shredded Cheese" _note="1/2 cup" />
                <outline text="Olive Oil, Salt, and Pepper" />
                <outline text="Strainer, Small Bowl, Medium Bowl, Baking Sheet, Paper Towel" />
              </outline>
              <outline text="Directions">
                <outline text="Prep">
                  <outline text="Adjust rack to top position and preheat broiler to high (or oven to 500 degrees). " />
                  <outline text="Wash and dry all produce. " />
                  <outline text="Dice tomato (into medium bowl)" />
                  <outline text="Chop cilantro leaves and stems, keeping them separate. " />
                  <outline text="Deseed and finely dice jalapeño. " />
                  <outline text="Zest and quarter lime. Halve, peel, and dice onion. " />
                  <outline text="Particularly Drain beans, reserving liquid in a small bowl." />
                  <outline text="" />
                </outline>
                <outline text="Make Salsa and Crema">
                  <outline text="Grab a medium and a small bowl." />
                  <outline text="In a medium bowl, combine tomato, cilantro leaves, half the jalapeño, juice from 2 lime wedges, and 2 TBSP onion; season with salt and pepper." />
                  <outline text="In a second small bowl, combine sour cream and lime zest (to taste). " />
                  <outline text="Stir in water, 1 tsp at a time, until mixture reaches a drizzling consistency. " />
                  <outline text="Season with salt and pepper." />
                  <outline text="" />
                </outline>
                <outline text="Mash Black Beans">
                  <outline text="Heat a large drizzle of oil in a medium pot over medium-high heat. " />
                  <outline text="Add remaining onion and cook, stirring, until softened, 2-3 minutes. " />
                  <outline text="Add beans, chili powder, and cilantro stems. " />
                  <outline text="Cook, stirring, until fragrant and thoroughly combined, 2-3 minutes. " />
                  <outline text="Add bean liquid and a pinch of salt. " />
                  <outline text="Cook until thickened, 4-5 minutes. " />
                  <outline text="Turn off heat; mash beans until mostly smooth." />
                  <outline text="" />
                </outline>
                <outline text="Char Corn">
                  <outline text="Meanwhile, drain corn and pat dry with paper towels." _note="(TIP: The drier your corn, the less likely it is to pop.) " />
                  <outline text="Heat a large dry pan over medium-high heat. " />
                  <outline text="Add corn and cook, without stirring, until browned on bottom, about 4 minutes. " />
                  <outline text="Add 1 TBSP Southwest Spice and a pinch of salt and pepper. " />
                  <outline text="Continue to cook, stirring, until browned all over, about 1 minute more. " />
                  <outline text="Turn off heat; transfer to a second medium bowl." />
                  <outline text="" />
                </outline>
                <outline text="Crisp Tortillas">
                  <outline text="Place tortillas on a baking sheet. " />
                  <outline text="Drizzle on both sides with olive oil; rub all over to coat. " />
                  <outline text="Poke all over with a fork. " />
                  <outline text="Broil, flipping halfway through, until lightly browned, 1-2 minutes per side." _note="TIP: Tortillas brown quickly! Keep a close eye on them." />
                  <outline text="" />
                </outline>
                <outline text="Assemble Tostadas">
                  <outline text="Spread tortillas with beans. " />
                  <outline text="Evenly top with cheese, corn, salsa, crema, and remaining jalapeño (to taste). " />
                  <outline text="Serve with remaining lime wedges on the side for squeezing over." />
                  <outline text="" />
                </outline>
              </outline>
              <outline text="Directions #copy">
                <outline text="Char Corn">
                  <outline text="Meanwhile, drain corn and pat dry with paper towels." _note="(TIP: The drier your corn, the less likely it is to pop.) " />
                  <outline text="Heat a large dry pan over medium-high heat. " />
                  <outline text="Add corn and cook, without stirring, until browned on bottom, about 4 minutes. " />
                  <outline text="Add 1 TBSP Southwest Spice and a pinch of salt and pepper. " />
                  <outline text="Continue to cook, stirring, until browned all over, about 1 minute more. " />
                  <outline text="Turn off heat; transfer to a second medium bowl." />
                  <outline text="" />
                </outline>
                <outline text="Crisp Tortillas">
                  <outline text="Place tortillas on a baking sheet. " />
