        <outline text="Monthly Country Food Runs">
          <outline text="Calendar" _note="Pick a country a month">
            <outline text="French Food" _note="January 2022">
              <outline text="Onion stew" />
              <outline text="Ratatouille" />
              <outline text="Coq au vin" />
              <outline text="Crepes" />
              <outline text="French foods to try (maybe) in January">
                <outline text="Cream Puff( the French are strong believers in stews/soups and pastries and that’s it)" />
                <outline text="The onion soup and the ratatouille are both vegetarian/ peasant dishes and comfort foods so they fit two of my criteria and crepes and coq au vin are infamous French foods" />
              </outline>
            </outline>
            <outline text="Chilean Food" _note="February 2022">
              <outline text="Drink that starts with an H" />
            </outline>
            <outline text="Ireland" _note="March 2022" />
            <outline text="Italy" _note="April 2022" />
          </outline>
          <outline text="Runs">
            <outline text="1. Dumplings from around the world " />
            <outline text="2. A classic dish from around the world " />
            <outline text="3. A comfort dish from around the world " />
            <outline text="4. A dessert from a different country" />
          </outline>
          <outline text="Links" _note="I have given several links for food runs.">
            <outline text="&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.tasteofhome.com/collection/travel-around-the-world-in-80-meals/&quot;&gt;https://www.tasteofhome.com/collection/travel-around-the-world-in-80-meals/&lt;/a&gt;" />
            <outline text="&lt;a href=&quot;https://tasty.co/article/hannahloewentheil/heres-what-comfort-food-looks-like-around-the-world&quot;&gt;https://tasty.co/article/hannahloewentheil/heres-what-comfort-food-looks-like-around-the-world&lt;/a&gt;" />
            <outline text="&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.thespruceeats.com/comfort-food-dishes-from-around-the-world-5112909&quot;&gt;https://www.thespruceeats.com/comfort-food-dishes-from-around-the-world-5112909&lt;/a&gt;" />
            <outline text="&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.insider.com/comfort-food-around-the-world-2018-3#fish-and-chips-is-the-comfort-food-of-great-britain-5&quot;&gt;https://www.insider.com/comfort-food-around-the-world-2018-3#fish-and-chips-is-the-comfort-food-of-great-britain-5&lt;/a&gt;" />
            <outline text="&lt;a href=&quot;https://travel.earth/try-these-35-delicious-types-of-dumplings-around-the-world/&quot;&gt;https://travel.earth/try-these-35-delicious-types-of-dumplings-around-the-world/&lt;/a&gt;" />
          </outline>
        </outline>
        <outline text="Planning Groceries in WorkFlowy">
          <outline text="About">
            <outline text="Workflowy can help us save time from scraping recipes ingredients into a grocery list by us already having our recipes in WF, then copying out those ingredients into our weekly grocery list." />
            <outline text="&lt;b&gt;Benefits&lt;/b&gt; of this method:">
              <outline text="&lt;b&gt;Save time &lt;/b&gt;creating grocery lists." _note="&lt;i&gt;As they are pre-listed with all required ingredients.&lt;/i&gt;" />
              <outline text="Know what recipe each ingredient is from (via color). 👌" _note="&quot;Why do we need three packs of tomatoes?&quot; Now we know. 🤯" />
              <outline text="Check off ingredients as you buy them. ✓" _note="Swipe right ➡️" />
              <outline text="&lt;b&gt;Waste less&lt;/b&gt; by verifying what foods we already have in the fridge/pantry." _note="Things with the #check_pantry tag are to be checked before going to the store.&#10;" />
              <outline text="Easily adjust which store you're buying that item from." _note="Just drag the ingredient down to the next store's list&#10;" />
            </outline>
            <outline text="Kyle volunteers to make sure that each week's ingredients and are loaded into our WorkFlowy Grocery List." _note="Ariel didn't like this step. She felt like she was being micromanaged.&#10;" />
            <outline text="Groceries are tagged with what store they come from. #ALDI " _note="This allows us to be able to trace which recipe that ingredient comes from. 👏" />
          </outline>
          <outline text="Meal Planning 💻">
            <outline text="&lt;b&gt;Decide&lt;/b&gt; what we're eating each night (together)">
              <outline text="Typically we'll do this per month." />
              <outline text="Don't forget to plan &lt;b&gt;lunches&lt;/b&gt; and &lt;b&gt;breakfasts&lt;/b&gt; too!" />
              <outline text="Mark the date in the recipe's note" _note="If following along with Ariel's paper calendar&#10;">
                <outline text="Example:">
                  <outline text="Chicken Dish" _note="&lt;u&gt;&lt;time startYear=&quot;2022&quot; startMonth=&quot;2&quot; startDay=&quot;12&quot;&gt;Sat, Feb 12, 2022&lt;/time&gt;&lt;/u&gt; " />
                </outline>
              </outline>
            </outline>
            <outline text="&lt;b&gt;Mirror&lt;/b&gt; each recipe to Menu for the Week." _note="&lt;b&gt;Shift + Drag Bullet &lt;/b&gt;to mirror, &lt;i&gt;or choose mirror in the bullet's menu&lt;/i&gt;">
              <outline text="Recipes &amp;gt; Menu">
                <outline text="Recipes 📇" />
                <outline text="&lt;b&gt;Menu &lt;/b&gt;for the Week" />
              </outline>
            </outline>
            <outline text="&lt;b&gt;Verify&lt;/b&gt; ingredients">
              <outline text="Confirm all meals ingredients are listed in &lt;a href=&quot;https://workflowy.com/#/44a962f3d032&quot;&gt;Menu for the Week&lt;/a&gt;." _note="All meals listed in the Meal area should be mirrored from the Recipe section." />
              <outline text="Make sure ingredients are tagged and formatted correctly.">
                <outline text="Good (Store Tag + Measurement in the note)">
                  <outline text="Sugar" _note="1/2 cup, #ALDI " />
                </outline>
                <outline text="Bad">
                  <outline text="1/2 a cup of sugar" />
                </outline>
              </outline>
            </outline>
            <outline text="&lt;b&gt;&lt;mark class=&quot;colored c-gray&quot;&gt;Clean Up&lt;/mark&gt;&lt;/b&gt;" _note="&lt;mark class=&quot;colored c-gray&quot;&gt;Delete out any pre-existing &quot;completed&quot; items in the Shopping List 🛒&lt;/mark&gt;">
              <outline text="&lt;a href=&quot;https://workflowy.com/#/78b5c6f5785c&quot;&gt;Shopping List 🛒 Grocery &lt;/a&gt;" />
            </outline>
            <outline text="&lt;b&gt;Copy&lt;/b&gt; &lt;mark class=&quot;colored c-red&quot;&gt;(not mirror) &lt;/mark&gt;the &quot;ingredients&quot; bullet into the “Shopping List” area.">
              <outline text="Meals &amp;gt; Shopping List" _note="Use this to &lt;b&gt;copy&lt;/b&gt; ingredients to the Grocery List. &#10;Ctrl + Drag to Duplicate  (Mac: Alt + Drag)&#10;">
                <outline text="Meals" />
                <outline text="Shopping List 🛒 Grocery " />
              </outline>
              <outline text="Tip: Keep them in the ingredients node until Friday (in case plans change)" />
            </outline>
            <outline text="&lt;b&gt;Color-code&lt;/b&gt; each dish">
              <outline text="Highlight all the ingredients and apply a color to them." />
              <outline text="Add that dishes name to the main shopping list node's note. " />
              <outline text="Hyperlink the meal text within the note at the top to &quot;&lt;b&gt;search is:color within Shopping List&lt;/b&gt;&quot; + View Meal Plan to go back to all meals for that week." />
            </outline>
            <outline text="&lt;b&gt;Add &lt;/b&gt;in any staples:">
              <outline text="Milk" />
              <outline text="Chocolate Milk" />
            </outline>
            <outline text="&lt;b&gt;Mark&lt;/b&gt; items with the #check_pantry tag, then use that filtered list to verify if we have those ingredients on-hand already or not. ">
              <outline text="Check the pantry&lt;b&gt; &lt;/b&gt;before heading to the store." />
              <outline text="Remove items we already have from the &lt;a href=&quot;https://workflowy.com/#/78b5c6f5785c?q=%23check_pantry%20&quot;&gt;Shopping List 🛒&lt;/a&gt;. " />
              <outline text="Also a great time to &lt;b&gt;throw away&lt;/b&gt; spoiled food. 😉" />
            </outline>
            <outline text="Update the chalkboard calendar (Ariel)" _note="Review/process each dish mentally by writing them on the chalkboard calendar.&#10;" />
            <outline text="&lt;b&gt;Organize&lt;/b&gt;" _note="Drag ingredients to their proper store list.">
              <outline text="Rearrange Ingredients to match store layout" _note="Wait to do this last...like on Friday">
                <outline text="Ideally, (click the store tag to filter) and move them into that store's list." />
              </outline>
              <outline text="For ingredients that already have a store tag, clicking the tag will filter out results, allowing you to drag 'em all at once. How nice!" />
            </outline>
          </outline>
          <outline text="Ideas">
            <outline text="Keep the recipes in their meal ingredients node (until Friday)" _note="That way if plans shift we can easily just remove a whole meal's ingredients.&#10;" />
            <outline text="&lt;b&gt;Update Store Tags&lt;/b&gt;. Look for new isle tags from last week's recipes to share across &lt;b&gt;all&lt;/b&gt; recipes via search." />
          </outline>
          <outline text="Questions">
            <outline text="Would it be helpful to dedicate the last Saturday of the month (or whatever day) to plan the next month's meals together?" />
            <outline text="Do you think a fridge cleanout before shopping could cut down on unnecessary cheeses, etc?" />
            <outline text="Do you find it helpful when I populate the grocery lists in WF each week?">
              <outline text="Undecided. Too much assistance has been perceived as micromanaging and Ari's lack of control of the dinner process." />
              <outline text="Is there anything I could do to improve this process?" />
            </outline>
          </outline>
        </outline>
